            PaneBox[
             DynamicBox[
              FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
              "FEBitmaps", "PauseButtonLargeHover"][Automatic]], ImageSize -> 
             40], Image`InteractiveDump`play$$ === False, 
            PaneBox[
             DynamicBox[
              FEPrivate`FrontEndResource["FEBitmaps", "PlayButtonLarge"][
              Automatic]], ImageSize -> 40], True, ""],
           ImageSizeCache->{4., {0., 0.}}],
          Alignment->Center,
          ImageSize->{640, 337}]}],
        EventHandlerTag[{{"MouseClicked", 1} :> 
          FEPrivate`Set[Image`InteractiveDump`play$$, 
            Not[Image`InteractiveDump`play$$]], "MouseEntered" :> 
          FEPrivate`Set[Image`InteractiveDump`hover$$, True], "MouseExited" :> 
          FEPrivate`Set[Image`InteractiveDump`hover$$, False], Method -> 
          "Preemptive", PassEventsDown -> Automatic, PassEventsUp -> True}]],
       BaseStyle->{ContextMenu -> {
           MenuItem["Play/Pause", 
            KernelExecute[
            Image`InteractiveDump`play$$ = Not[Image`InteractiveDump`play$$]],
             MenuEvaluator -> Automatic], 
           MenuItem["Stop", 
            KernelExecute[
            Image`InteractiveDump`play$$ = False; Image`Utilities`i$$ = 1], 
            MenuEvaluator -> Automatic], Delimiter, 
           Menu["Frame Rate", {
             MenuItem["8", 
              KernelExecute[Image`InteractiveDump`rate$$ = 8], MenuEvaluator -> 
              Automatic], 
             MenuItem["16", 
              KernelExecute[Image`InteractiveDump`rate$$ = 16], MenuEvaluator -> 
              Automatic], 
             MenuItem["24", 
              KernelExecute[Image`InteractiveDump`rate$$ = 24], MenuEvaluator -> 
              Automatic], 
             MenuItem["30", 
              KernelExecute[Image`InteractiveDump`rate$$ = 30], MenuEvaluator -> 
              Automatic], 
             MenuItem["50", 
              KernelExecute[Image`InteractiveDump`rate$$ = 50], MenuEvaluator -> 
              Automatic], 
             MenuItem["60", 
              KernelExecute[Image`InteractiveDump`rate$$ = 60], MenuEvaluator -> 
              Automatic]}]}, Selectable -> False},
       DynamicModuleValues:>{}],
      BoxForm`AnimatedImageTag[
      FrameRate -> 1.25, AnimationRunning -> True, AnimationRepetitions -> 
       DirectedInfinity[1]]]},
    {
     PaneBox[
      StyleBox["\<\"Cover animation.  15-month time-lapse of the NOAA ERSSTv5 \
monthly SST anomaly field over the tropical Pacific (Feb 2025 \[Rule] Apr \
2026), overlaid at 65 % opacity on Wolfram's built-in satellite imagery. The \
Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 monitoring box is outlined in yellow at the equator; the \
current basin-mean Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 anomaly appears in the upper-left badge. \
Watch the 2024\[Dash]25 La Ni\[NTilde]a cold tongue dissolve through autumn \
2025, then the central Pacific warm through winter and propagate eastward \
through spring 2026. The full code that produced this animation is given in \
\[Section]3.5.\"\>",
       StripOnInput->False,
       FontFamily->"Helvetica",
       FontSize->10,
       FontSlant->Italic,
       FontColor->GrayLevel[0.35]],
      Alignment->Center,
      ImageSize->640]}
   },
   DefaultBaseStyle->"Column",
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Center}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Column"]], "Output",
 CellMargins->{{Automatic, Automatic}, {10, 14}},
 ShowCellLabel->False,
 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"90644e84-3f02-4037-b5e5-5415d168378c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"211c00db-8ea5-4bd5-98a8-8f176bb78b4a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "NOAA's Climate Prediction Center currently has an ",
 StyleBox["El Ni\[NTilde]o Watch",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " in effect. The May 2026 ENSO Diagnostic Discussion gives a ",
 StyleBox["~82% probability",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of El Ni\[NTilde]o onset during May\[Dash]July 2026 and a ",
 StyleBox["~96% probability",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " that the event persists through DJF 2026\[Dash]27. The tropical Pacific \
has just emerged from a weak La Ni\[NTilde]a, and the equatorial cold tongue \
is warming sharply (Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 anomaly climbed from \[Minus]0.67 \
\[Degree]C in December 2025 to +0.23 \[Degree]C in April 2026)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.98, 0.96, 0.9],ExpressionUUID->"d8f75490-a1ae-478f-8155-e414ee96c3f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook does three things. First, it ",
 StyleBox["pulls the live data",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 monthly anomalies from NOAA PSL, the Oceanic \
Ni\[NTilde]o Index from CPC, the IRI/CPC forecast plume, and the CPC \
probability table) in pure Wolfram Language. Second, it computes the ",
 StyleBox["spring predictability barrier",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " directly from 77 years of observations, showing how forecasts initialised \
in January lose almost all skill by July, while forecasts initialised in July \
retain skill through the following winter. Third, it implements ",
 StyleBox["two textbook coupled ocean\[Dash]atmosphere toy models",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] Jin's (1997) recharge\[Dash]discharge oscillator and Suarez & \
Schopf's (1988) delayed-action oscillator \[LongDash] and uses them to \
reproduce the barrier mechanism and to produce a toy-model live forecast cone \
for the developing 2026 event."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.98, 0.96, 0.9],ExpressionUUID->"cac297ca-7109-45dc-9f8e-3609034f0119"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Audience:",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the prose is written for two overlapping audiences. Each section opens \
with an intuitive explanation that requires no background, then deepens into \
a quantitative treatment with equations, numerical integration code, and 5-95 \
% / 25-75 % confidence intervals. Climate scientists will recognise the \
canonical references; general readers should be able to follow the \
geophysical narrative."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.98, 0.96, 0.9],ExpressionUUID->"2fa62557-2cc5-4106-9cf0-10757e19ea35"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup (optional \[LongDash] only needed if you want to run the code)", \
"Section",ExpressionUUID->"47d335ef-5308-4f22-aed0-b0d977099e8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["You can ignore this section entirely if you just want to read the \
post.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " Every figure is pre-rendered into the notebook as a static image, so the \
prose, equations, and figures all work without evaluating anything."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"5665bcd9-916e-44ee-b56a-a4917563e9c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If you ",
 StyleBox["do",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " want to run the code cells, the simulation helpers \
(recharge\[Dash]discharge oscillator, Suarez\[Dash]Schopf delayed oscillator, \
ensemble forecasters, hero-animation renderer, live-data loaders) live in a \
single attached package, ",
 StyleBox["enso_emergence_helpers.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", uploaded alongside the notebook. Run the cell below once after opening \
the notebook; it loads every helper symbol used in the rest of the post."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"f28d8625-c060-4ee1-97a6-abb0fa30666b"],

Cell["\<\
(* Attach the helper package -- put enso_emergence_helpers.wl in
   the same folder as this notebook and shift-Enter the line below. *)
SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Get[\"enso_emergence_helpers.wl\"];\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"7b74be53-80fb-4355-a482-08776789b2a9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.  What is ENSO?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"78462add-edf1-432a-9125-91b23d777cfd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The basic facts.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " The El Ni\[NTilde]o\[Dash]Southern Oscillation (ENSO) is the largest \
source of year-to-year climate variability on Earth. It lives in the tropical \
Pacific and consists of two halves that are physically inseparable: ",
 StyleBox["El Ni\[NTilde]o",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", a sloshing of warm water from the western to the central and eastern \
equatorial Pacific (warmer-than-usual sea surface temperatures in the \
central/eastern basin), and ",
 StyleBox["La Ni\[NTilde]a",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", the opposite phase, in which the warm pool retreats westward and the \
eastern Pacific cold tongue intensifies. The whole system oscillates on a \
3-to-7-year time scale and is the dominant driver of global inter-annual \
atmospheric variability."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"30f4581e-4ae8-4f76-83d3-13c0c5972133"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ENSO state is conventionally measured by the SST anomaly (departure \
from the climatological mean) in one of four \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Ni\
\[NTilde]o boxes\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in the equatorial Pacific. The \
most-watched box is ",
 StyleBox["Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (5\[Degree]N\[Dash]5\[Degree]S, 170\[Degree]W\[Dash]120\[Degree]W), \
straddling the dateline. NOAA's operational definition of an El Ni\[NTilde]o \
event is that the three-month running mean of the Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 anomaly \
(the ",
 StyleBox["Oceanic Ni\[NTilde]o Index",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ", ONI) exceeds +0.5 \[Degree]C for five consecutive overlapping seasons."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"5ab01ebe-3d57-4ef7-9997-6d30c86ea6ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["External asset.",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ",
 "Figure 1.1",
 " was generated outside Wolfram Language with OpenAI's ",
 StyleBox["gpt-image-2",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " model (the prompts and a one-off Python driver are checked into ",
 StyleBox["docs/images/figures-generated/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " of the project repository). It is included as a static illustration; there \
is no WL code to run for this figure. See \[Section]9 Acknowledgements for \
the licence."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {6, 4}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.45, 0.55, 0.7],
 FontSize->11,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.88, 0.91, 0.95],ExpressionUUID->"28933548-e0e8-4c71-9051-2001ed5fb1d2"],

