Cell["\<\
Figure 1.2  Schematic of the climatological Walker circulation along the \
equator. Easterly trade winds at the surface, rising air over the Indonesian \
warm pool, upper-level westerly return flow, descending air over the cool \
eastern Pacific. During El Ni\[NTilde]o the trades weaken, the thermocline \
flattens, and the rising branch shifts east toward the dateline. Generated \
with OpenAI gpt-image-2.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"8eecd89f-afb5-45c5-b69f-719caad3446c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.  The May 2026 El Ni\[NTilde]o Watch", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ecfe14dc-0fe0-4ccc-bedd-fda96f004ed0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "NOAA's Climate Prediction Center and Columbia's IRI jointly issue an ENSO \
Diagnostic Discussion at the start of each month. The discussion is a prose \
document combined with the IRI/CPC plume of ~25 dynamical and statistical \
model forecasts. When the official probability of El Ni\[NTilde]o onset \
within the next few seasons exceeds ~55 %, the CPC raises an ",
 StyleBox["El Ni\[NTilde]o Watch",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "; when it exceeds ~70 %, a Watch is escalated to an ",
 StyleBox["Advisory",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (similar logic for La Ni\[NTilde]a)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"b1d83a41-3d3b-4569-b043-379b2248e2fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Popular-science take.",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " The BBC's lead weather presenter Simon King has a 5-minute explainer on \
the same emerging event \[LongDash] \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Right now, across \
the Pacific Ocean, something is happening that could change the world's \
weather.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]  He notes that US, Australian, and European \
forecasters all see this El Ni\[NTilde]o forming within the next month, with \
a 2-in-3 chance of becoming strong or very strong by late autumn / early \
winter, and around half of the European model runs suggesting it could be one \
of the strongest on record. Some forecasters have already nicknamed it the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Godzilla\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] El Ni\[NTilde]o. ",
 StyleBox["BBC News explainer (Simon King)",
  FontWeight->"SemiBold"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UEseLvpl9ss",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->10],
 ")",
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{0, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[0.93, 0.95, 0.99],
 FrameMargins -> 12,ExpressionUUID->"bf5b493e-43c3-45b3-8e7d-e712cd868230"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The May 2026 issuance is unambiguous. The probability bars below show El Ni\
\[NTilde]o probabilities climbing from 82 % in May\[Dash]June\[Dash]July 2026 \
to 96 % in the four overlapping seasons straddling DJF 2026\[Dash]27, with La \
Ni\[NTilde]a essentially ruled out until early 2027. The bar chart is built \
directly from the snapshot JSON written by ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/fetch_cpc_probabilities.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"23f319fc-e5d4-421a-be4a-6a4c4be9df01"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(* Figure 2.1: NOAA / IRI ENSO probability bars.
   LoadProbSnapshot[] is in enso_emergence_helpers.wl (the package
   loaded by the Setup cell). It returns a hand-curated snapshot of
   the May-2026 CPC bar chart; there is no machine-readable CPC feed. *)
probData = LoadProbSnapshot[];
{seasons, laNina, neutral, elNino} = Transpose[
   {#[\"season\"], #[\"la_nina\"], #[\"neutral\"], #[\"el_nino\"]} & /@
   probData[\"probabilities\"]];
probBars = BarChart[
   Transpose[{laNina, neutral, elNino}],
   ChartLayout -> \"Stacked\",
   ChartStyle -> {RGBColor[0.20, 0.45, 0.75],   (* La Ni\[CapitalATilde]\
\[PlusMinus]a blue *)
                  RGBColor[0.6, 0.6, 0.6],      (* Neutral grey *)
                  RGBColor[0.83, 0.32, 0.10]},  (* El Ni\[CapitalATilde]\
\[PlusMinus]o red  *)
   ChartLabels -> {Style[#, FontSize -> 9] & /@ seasons, None},
   ChartLegends -> Placed[
     {\"La Ni\\[NTilde]a\", \"Neutral\", \"El Ni\\[NTilde]o\"}, Right],
   Frame -> True,
   FrameLabel -> {{\"probability (%)\", None},
                  {\"rolling 3-month season\", None}},
   PlotRange -> {Automatic, {0, 100}},
   AspectRatio -> 0.45, ImageSize -> 900]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"3347c446-17a9-4fd2-9aaa-5f90ba27cfbd"],

