Cell["\<\
Figure 2.2  The full monthly Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 SST anomaly record from NOAA \
PSL (ERSSTv5 dataset, base period 1991\[Dash]2020). The four \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]super-El-Ni\[NTilde]o\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] events \
(1982\[Dash]83, 1997\[Dash]98, 2015\[Dash]16, 2023\[Dash]24) are clearly \
visible as the > +2 \[Degree]C peaks. The right edge of the record is the \
warming we are about to forecast.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"737daf38-92e6-45df-a63e-ed8792d3ac51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What the data show right now.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " The most recent four months of Ni\[NTilde]o 3.4 anomalies, fetched live \
for this notebook, are:"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4fe6a1c7-8a0d-4599-b84d-e4ed550ffdf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["November 2025",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "    ",
 StyleBox["-0.70 \[Degree]C",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["December 2025",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "    ",
 StyleBox["-0.67 \[Degree]C",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["January 2026",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "    ",
 StyleBox["-0.58 \[Degree]C",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["February 2026",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "    ",
 StyleBox["-0.27 \[Degree]C",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["March 2026",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "    ",
 StyleBox["-0.01 \[Degree]C",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["April 2026",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "    ",
 StyleBox["0.23 \[Degree]C",
  FontFamily->"Courier"]
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{100, 100}, {6, 6}},
 FontFamily->"Helvetica",
 FontSize->13,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"5cd2af7c-2dfb-408b-9f18-cb8e86cca424"],

Cell["\<\
The +0.50 \[Degree]C jump from February to April (\[Minus]0.27 \[RightArrow] \
+0.23) sits comfortably in the top decile of all Feb\[Dash]Apr changes since \
1950 (ranked 9th of 77, tied with 1963 \[LongDash] the top three are 1951 at \
+0.81, 2014 at +0.70, and 2000 at +0.68). It is exactly the kind of emergent \
behaviour that the toy models in \[Section]5 are designed to capture: a \
stochastic system on the edge of bifurcation, given a favourable phase-space \
starting point by the upper-ocean heat content left over from previous La Ni\
\[NTilde]a recharge, gets a spring westerly-wind-burst kick and launches into \
the growth regime.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"1faac8c0-cc9b-4963-a28e-9af3c54fa6e9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3.  Why ENSO matters: global teleconnections", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ee598d47-177a-4cff-b758-fc026a225e12"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "ENSO is not just a Pacific story. The warm pool's eastward shift during El \
Ni\[NTilde]o reorganises tropical convection, which launches stationary \
Rossby-wave trains into the extratropics, which in turn shift the jet streams \
and the storm tracks across the entire Northern Hemisphere winter. These ",
 StyleBox["teleconnections",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " are strong enough to be statistically detectable and operationally useful \
for seasonal forecasting on every continent."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"f45b0989-eef2-42e4-a1a4-6dd541deea59"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["External asset.",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ",
 "Figure 3.1",
 " was generated outside Wolfram Language with OpenAI's ",
 StyleBox["gpt-image-2",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " model (the prompts and a one-off Python driver are checked into ",
 StyleBox["docs/images/figures-generated/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " of the project repository). It is included as a static illustration; there \
is no WL code to run for this figure. See \[Section]9 Acknowledgements for \
the licence."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {6, 4}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.45, 0.55, 0.7],
 FontSize->11,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.88, 0.91, 0.95],ExpressionUUID->"d2b82e58-63d7-4f25-bd19-6113e79eb83f"],

