Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 4.3  Persistence-skill curves: ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho]",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " vs lead for each starting calendar month. Lines that start in boreal \
winter and spring (Jan, Feb, Mar, Apr) drop steeply through the first six \
leads; lines that start in summer and autumn (Jul, Aug, Sep, Oct) retain ",
 StyleBox["\[Rho] > 0.5",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " out to lead 9."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"069e76b0-657c-4831-90f3-2173f4b8b556"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why the barrier exists.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " There are three reinforcing mechanisms. (a) The Bjerknes feedback ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"R", "(", "t", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8945c283-b722-46d8-9d67-569a96e91ca2"],
 " (the coupled-system growth rate that we will derive in \[Section]5.1) is \
seasonally modulated. It is strongest in boreal autumn, when the \
climatological cold tongue and trade winds are most pronounced, and weakest \
\[LongDash] often near zero or slightly negative \[LongDash] in boreal \
spring, when the cold tongue retreats and the intertropical convergence zone \
(ITCZ) sits near the equator. A small initial-condition perturbation in \
spring is therefore not amplified by coupling; it just sits there or decays."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"49c7dbf0-df60-44fe-b7ec-696a2b4faf70"],

Cell["\<\
(b) Westerly-wind-burst (WWB) activity in the western Pacific peaks in March\
\[Dash]April. The injected stochastic forcing dominates the deterministic \
dynamics during this season, washing out the information carried by the \
initial condition.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"b9d304ff-c972-49a9-aad3-5fb32604c5a7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "(c) The thermocline phase relationship between ",
 StyleBox["T",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["h",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (eastern SST and western thermocline depth) goes through a transition in \
spring: the system is in transit between the recharged and discharged states \
of the canonical recharge\[Dash]discharge cycle. Small phase errors compound \
here."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"bd4a576a-0113-4bb2-a87b-e9ab006191f0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.  Two toy models of ENSO", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"001d8f63-5701-42d6-814a-3ec16524ce1b"],

Cell["\<\
There is a remarkable two-fold reduction of the full coupled \
ocean\[Dash]atmosphere problem that produces tractable models exhibiting the \
essential ENSO physics. Both reductions are pre-PNAS-era classical references \
and both can be implemented in under 100 lines of Wolfram Language.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"3bbd7d05-c09a-41ae-ad2a-f0ef56b9430f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Cell-evaluation order in this section.",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontSlant->Italic],
 "  The wlIn cells below carry forward a few variables so each one runs on \
top of the previous. To re-run a single figure you need the upstream cells \
live in the same kernel: ",
 StyleBox["samp",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is defined in Figure 5.3 and reused in Figure 5.4; ",
 StyleBox["forecastEnsemble[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is called separately in Figures 5.5 and 5.6 (no cross-dependency); ",
 StyleBox["simulateDDE[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " in 5.8 and ",
 StyleBox["forecastEnsembleDDE[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " in 5.9 stand on their own. If you skipped ahead, just shift-Enter the \
earlier cell first."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {6, 4}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.78, 0.55, 0.15],
 FontSize->11,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0.25],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.97, 0.92, 0.78],ExpressionUUID->"6204327b-590f-4182-be99-864a39b7ef21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["External asset.",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " ",
 "Figure 5.1",
 " was generated outside Wolfram Language with OpenAI's ",
 StyleBox["gpt-image-2",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " model (the prompts and a one-off Python driver are checked into ",
 StyleBox["docs/images/figures-generated/",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " of the project repository). It is included as a static illustration; there \
is no WL code to run for this figure. See \[Section]9 Acknowledgements for \
the licence."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {6, 4}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.45, 0.55, 0.7],
 FontSize->11,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0.3],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.88, 0.91, 0.95],ExpressionUUID->"1af6ffda-905d-48d5-a115-828d379663e6"],

